  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Find the largest interval of continuity for the function $f(x)={log}_{3}\u2061(\\frac{x-2}{{5}^{x}}).$",
  "worked_solution": "Our function is a logarithmic function, so it is continuous over all points in its domain.\n\nTo find the domain of ${log}_{3}\u2061(\\frac{x-2}{{5}^{x}}),$ we set the expression under the logarithm to be greater than zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-2}{{5}^{x}}>0\\,\u27f9\\,x-2>0\\,\u27f9\\,x>2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $f(x)={log}_{3}\u2061(\\frac{x-2}{{5}^{x}})$ is $(2,\\infty ),$ and it is also continuous on this interval.",
